WEBVTT

00:00.320 --> 00:01.650
- [Instructor] We're told Sloan went

00:01.650 --> 00:03.770
on a four-day hiking trip.

00:03.770 --> 00:07.080
Each day, she walked 20%
more than the distance

00:07.080 --> 00:09.540
that she walked the day before.

00:09.540 --> 00:13.000
She walked a total of 27 kilometers.

00:13.000 --> 00:15.080
What is the distance Sloan walked

00:15.080 --> 00:16.840
in the first day of the trip?

00:16.840 --> 00:18.410
And it says to round our final answer

00:18.410 --> 00:19.640
to the nearest kilometer.

00:19.640 --> 00:21.900
So, like always, have a go with this

00:21.900 --> 00:22.840
and see if you can figure out

00:22.840 --> 00:25.163
how much she walked on the first day.

00:26.050 --> 00:27.670
All right, well let's just call the amount

00:27.670 --> 00:30.150
that she walked on the first day a.

00:30.150 --> 00:33.190
And then using a, let's
see if we can set up

00:33.190 --> 00:36.320
an expression for how
much she walked in total.

00:36.320 --> 00:38.720
And then, that should be equal to 27.

00:38.720 --> 00:41.760
And then hopefully, we're going
to be able to solve for a.

00:41.760 --> 00:44.970
So the first day, she walks a kilometers.

00:44.970 --> 00:46.610
Now, how about the second day?

00:46.610 --> 00:50.560
Well, they tell us that each
day, she walked 20% more

00:50.560 --> 00:53.270
than the distance she
walked the day before.

00:53.270 --> 00:56.020
So, on the next day, she's
going to walk 20% more

00:56.020 --> 01:01.020
than a kilometers, so that's 1.2 times a.

01:01.330 --> 01:04.800
And what about the day
after that, her third day?

01:04.800 --> 01:08.290
Well, that's just gonna be 1.2
times this, the second day,

01:08.290 --> 01:10.290
and so that's going to be 1.2 times 1.2,

01:12.468 --> 01:14.840
or we can say 1.2 squared times a.

01:15.770 --> 01:17.450
And then how much on the fourth day?

01:17.450 --> 01:19.180
And that's, she went on
a four-day hiking trip,

01:19.180 --> 01:20.920
so that's the last day.

01:20.920 --> 01:23.730
Well, that's gonna be
1.2 times the third day.

01:23.730 --> 01:28.190
So, that's going to be 1.2
to the third power times a.

01:28.190 --> 01:30.360
So, this is an expression in a

01:30.360 --> 01:32.520
on how much she walked over the four days.

01:32.520 --> 01:36.080
And we know that she walked
a total of 27 kilometers,

01:36.080 --> 01:39.350
so this is going to be
equal to 27 kilometers.

01:39.350 --> 01:42.580
Now, you could solve for a over here.

01:42.580 --> 01:44.570
You could factor out the a

01:44.570 --> 01:48.780
and you could say a times one plus 1.2

01:48.780 --> 01:53.610
plus 1.2 squared plus
1.2 to the third power

01:53.610 --> 01:55.130
is equal to 27.

01:55.130 --> 01:58.900
And then you could say
that a is equal to 27

01:58.900 --> 02:03.290
over one plus 1.2 plus 1.2 squared

02:03.290 --> 02:05.460
plus 1.2 to the third power,

02:05.460 --> 02:08.770
and we would need a
calculator to evaluate this.

02:08.770 --> 02:10.350
But I'm gonna do a different technique,

02:10.350 --> 02:13.690
a technique that would work
even if you had 20 terms here.

02:13.690 --> 02:16.140
You, in theory, could
also do this with 20 terms

02:16.140 --> 02:19.713
but it gets a lot more complicated,
or if you had 200 terms.

02:21.110 --> 02:22.740
So the other way to approach this

02:22.740 --> 02:26.860
is use the formula for a
finite geometric series.

02:26.860 --> 02:28.950
What does it evaluate to?

02:28.950 --> 02:31.440
And just as a reminder, the sum

02:32.420 --> 02:37.140
of first n terms,

02:37.140 --> 02:41.253
it's going to be the first
term, which we could call a,

02:42.200 --> 02:47.200
minus the first term
times our common ratio.

02:47.380 --> 02:49.660
In this case, our common ratio is 1.2

02:49.660 --> 02:53.110
because every successive
term is 1.2 times the first.

02:53.110 --> 02:57.040
So our first term times our
common ratio to the nth power,

02:57.040 --> 03:01.270
all of that over one
minus the common ratio.

03:01.270 --> 03:03.750
In other videos, we explain
where this comes from,

03:03.750 --> 03:06.200
we prove this, but here,
we can just apply it.

03:06.200 --> 03:08.930
We already know what our a is,
I used that as our variable.

03:08.930 --> 03:11.140
Our common ratio in this situation

03:11.140 --> 03:13.233
is going to be equal to 1.2.

03:14.520 --> 03:18.760
And our n is going to be equal to four.

03:18.760 --> 03:20.100
Another way I like to think about it

03:20.100 --> 03:23.670
is it's our first term, which
we see right over there,

03:23.670 --> 03:27.310
minus the term that we did not get to.

03:27.310 --> 03:29.120
If we were to have a fifth term,

03:29.120 --> 03:31.830
it would have been that fifth
term that we're subtracting

03:31.830 --> 03:34.090
because we aren't getting
to a fourth power here,

03:34.090 --> 03:35.970
the fifth term would have
been the fourth power,

03:35.970 --> 03:38.880
all of that over one
minus the common ratio.

03:38.880 --> 03:42.680
And so, this left-hand
side of our equation,

03:42.680 --> 03:46.360
we could rewrite as our first term

03:46.360 --> 03:50.760
minus our first term times
our common ratio, 1.2,

03:51.620 --> 03:53.750
to the fourth power.

03:53.750 --> 03:58.070
All of that over one
minus our common ratio.

03:58.070 --> 04:00.960
And then that could be equal to 27.

04:00.960 --> 04:02.300
Let me scroll down a little bit

04:02.300 --> 04:05.980
so we have some more
space to then solve this.

04:05.980 --> 04:09.143
And so, let's see, I can
simplify this a little bit.

04:10.210 --> 04:13.573
This is going to be equal to negative 0.2.

04:14.440 --> 04:17.210
Our numerator, we can factor out a.

04:17.210 --> 04:20.030
And so, this is going to be equal to a

04:20.030 --> 04:24.640
times one minus 1.2 to the fourth power.

04:24.640 --> 04:26.010
And let's see, we can multiply

04:26.010 --> 04:28.790
both the numerator and the
denominator by negative one.

04:28.790 --> 04:33.070
And so, this would get us to a times,

04:33.070 --> 04:36.580
a times, and I'll put the
a out of the fraction,

04:36.580 --> 04:38.500
a time, so I'll just swap the order here

04:38.500 --> 04:39.980
and get rid of this negative.

04:39.980 --> 04:43.110
1.2 to the fourth power minus one

04:43.110 --> 04:47.890
over 0.2 is equal to 27.

04:47.890 --> 04:51.130
Again, all I did is I took
the a out of the fraction

04:51.130 --> 04:53.560
so it's out here, and I multiplied

04:53.560 --> 04:55.120
the numerator and the
denominator by negative.

04:55.120 --> 04:57.810
The numerator multiplied by
negative would swap these two.

04:57.810 --> 05:00.530
And then multiplying
negative 0.2 times negative

05:00.530 --> 05:02.260
is just positive 0.2.

05:02.260 --> 05:05.190
And so now, I can just multiply both sides

05:05.190 --> 05:08.050
times the reciprocal of this.

05:08.050 --> 05:09.540
So, I'll do up here.

05:09.540 --> 05:14.190
So, 0.2 over 1.2 to the fourth minus one.

05:14.190 --> 05:18.140
And then here, 0.2 over

05:18.140 --> 05:21.410
1.2 to the fourth minus one.

05:21.410 --> 05:23.300
That cancels with that,
that cancels with that,

05:23.300 --> 05:24.760
that's exactly why I did that.

05:24.760 --> 05:28.380
And we're left with a is equal to,

05:28.380 --> 05:31.120
it is equal to, I'll
just write it in yellow,

05:31.120 --> 05:34.760
27 times 0.2,

05:34.760 --> 05:38.910
all of that over 1.2 to
the fourth minus one.

05:38.910 --> 05:40.520
And this expression should give us

05:40.520 --> 05:43.600
the exact same value as
that expression we just saw,

05:43.600 --> 05:45.730
but this is useful even
if we had a hundred terms,

05:45.730 --> 05:46.930
we could use this.

05:46.930 --> 05:49.380
And so, I'll get the calculator out.

05:49.380 --> 05:50.890
This will give us...

05:52.150 --> 05:55.370
So, actually, I'll evaluate
this denominator first,

05:55.370 --> 05:59.370
so I'll have 1.2 to the fourth power,

05:59.370 --> 06:02.650
which is equal to minus one, is equal to,

06:02.650 --> 06:03.920
and that's in the denominator,

06:03.920 --> 06:06.260
so I could just take the reciprocal of it,

06:06.260 --> 06:08.970
and then multiply that, times 27

06:09.840 --> 06:12.610
times 0.2

06:12.610 --> 06:15.070
is equal to 5.029.

06:15.070 --> 06:16.700
Now, they want us to round our answer

06:16.700 --> 06:17.950
to the nearest kilometer,

06:17.950 --> 06:21.810
so this is going to be
approximately equal to,

06:21.810 --> 06:23.950
approximately equal to five kilometers.

06:23.950 --> 06:27.440
That's how much approximately
that she would have traveled

06:27.440 --> 06:29.753
on the first day of her hiking trip.
